# Build output
/buddynet
/dist/
*.exe
# Compiled lab/pentest helpers. Each tool lives in a directory named after itself,
# so `go build` inside one drops a binary right next to its source — which is how
# a 4.5 MB executable once reached a commit. The labs build these into a temp dir;
# nothing in the tree should ever carry the compiled form.
/lab/pentest/applyscope/applyscope
/lab/pentest/labtool/labtool
/lab/pentest/probe/probe
/lab/pentest/relayflood/relayflood

# Local runtime state
*.key
peers.json
known_peers
*.pending

# Lab test environment — .env contains the generated server key, not for commit
/lab/.env
# Generated BuddyParty manifests — contain node keys + bootstrap tokens (re-created
# by setup-party.sh from the persistent key volumes), not for commit
/lab/party/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Claude Code / local working context — these live in the working tree for
# convenience but must NEVER be pushed to GitHub:
#   CLAUDE.md      repo guidance for Claude Code (kept local for this project)
#   .claude/       per-project Claude state, incl. a symlink to the memory store
#   docs/plans/    pre-agreed implementation plans (referenced from CLAUDE.md)
/CLAUDE.md
/.claude/
/docs/plans/
AGENTS.md
